  "notes": "Real RAD plastic (E) detector dose rate from MSL sol 4190 (product RAD_RDR_2024_140_18_30_4190_V00), linearly interpolated between observation centres (observations of 481 to 961 s). Onset (minutes_since_onset 0) is the start of the first observation above 1.5 times the pre-event baseline, 2024-05-20T05:21:50Z; the steep rise follows within about 15 minutes. The DONKI CME id marks the coronal mass ejection from a backsided active region, not the arrival time. uSv/h is an upper bound: absorbed dose times the surface quality factor 3.05 (Hassler et al. 2014), which is probably too high for solar energetic protons. Truncated observations were dropped. NASA reported 8,100 microgray for an astronaut next to Curiosity; this sol's dosimetry totals only about 1.3 to 1.6 mGy, so that figure is not reproduced here (unresolved, cite as NASA reported). Estimates, not measured dose equivalent."
